codex
Program fidelity is straightforward at the Python level: both implementations select indices `0,2,4,…` and sum values whose remainder modulo 2 is nonzero. I’m adding an independent, deterministic differential harness that covers all short lists over `[-3,3]`, explicit examples and edge cases, very large integers, and seeded longer inputs; it imports the trusted canonical implementation separately from the candidate.
